{
  "claim": "For non-headline series with one panel provider, infrequent middle-provider repricing and no active stability gate, fm2 alone will reduce pinball loss relative to the current analog forecast.",
  "mechanism": "The hypothesis is that these published medians move mainly through occasional repricing by the sole provider or changes in its offered inventory. Between those events, fm2's last-value centre and short context should better preserve the current price level than analog windows drawn across series.",
  "spec": {
    "when": {
      "all": [
        {"fact": "in37", "op": "==", "value": false},
        {"fact": "gate14", "op": "==", "value": false},
        {"fact": "has_panel", "op": "==", "value": true},
        {"fact": "p_providers", "op": "<", "value": 2},
        {"fact": "mid_prov_reprice21", "op": "<", "value": 0.0952}
      ]
    },
    "do": {
      "action": "members_only",
      "members": ["fm2"]
    }
  },
  "falsification": "Reject the rule if pooled skill fails to rise overall or in either selection half, fewer than 200 cells across at least five series change, headline skill falls, or fewer than 90% of the 2000 ISO-week block bootstrap resamples show improvement.",
  "prior_ids_used": [],
  "expects": "I expect a modest pooled-skill improvement with headline forecasts unchanged. The reported low-repricing, single-provider slice favors fm2 over the current system by 0.042 skill across 1918 cells and 70 series; the exact non-headline subset, gains in each half and bootstrap support remain to be tested."
}
